[AXIOM SCRIPT :: DIGITAL_TYPOLOGY_INTAKE :: v2.1]
// Compiled from digital-typology.xml v2.1. Phase 1 = trace (steps 1–12). Phase 2 = verification (steps 13–18).

@STATE_INIT:
  {Prompt}          := [User prompt text]                 // target or task; NULL → target = project folder
  {Target}          := [Project folder context]           // overridden only if {Prompt} names a target
  {Result_ID}       := GENERATE( unique id )              // never used internally; passed to intake.start; later pasted into digital-typology-expand.xml canonical_input
  {Intake_State}    := UNKNOWN                            // NONE | RECORDING | ACTIVE
  {Prompt_Mode}     := UNKNOWN                            // INTAKE | VERIFY_ONLY | REFINE | CORRECTION_LAYER | BLIND_SPOT | FEATURE | OTHER_TASK
  {Input_Kind}      := UNKNOWN                            // SINGLE_AUE | FOLDER_OR_COLLECTION
  {Phase}           := 1                                  // 1 = trace ; 2 = verification
  {Roots}           := { code, document, media, data, upstream, downstream, collection }
  {Roles}           := { AUE, CQU, DE, SE, NE }           // exactly one per element; PE is a join endpoint, not a role
  {Join_Types}      := { purpose }
  {IFD}             := { sends, receives, both }           // sends: OP→EF ; receives: EF→OP ; both: equal need
  {Conditions}      := { UNVERIFIED, OK, BKN, MISS }       // DEFAULT := UNVERIFIED. OK requires a read ref. BKN requires explanation + correction.
  {Ref_Member}      := { key := path,  value := [path_relative_to_project_root] }
  {Ref_Upstream}    := { key := sdk|library|service|api|protocol, value := [product_and_version] }
  {Ref_Read}        := { key := read,  value := [path#location] }                 // evidence: this source was read
  {Ref_Spec}        := { key := spec,  value := [specification_record] }          // governing spec record
  {Members}         := []                                  // every file in the project, listed once, used by both phases
  {Open_OPs}        := []                                  // unsatisfied Operative Purposes (phase 1 work queue)
  {Unverified}      := []                                  // elements with condition UNVERIFIED (phase 2 work queue)
  {Untouched}       := []                                  // members no ref touches (phase 2 coverage queue)
  {Set_Aside}       := {}                                  // member → one-line reason it is not notable
  {Recorded}        := {}                                  // namespace_address → element ; (receiver,provider) → join
  {Map_State}       := EMPTY                               // EMPTY | TRACING | CLOSED | ANNEALED | PROOFED_1 | VERIFYING | PROOFED_2
  {Report}          := { per_module: { read:[], set_aside:[], OK:0, BKN:0, MISS:0 }, partial := FALSE }
  {MCP}             := mcp.metaform.*

@CONSTRAINT:
  +> RECORD one object per tool call (intake.element / intake.join) AT THE MOMENT it is reasoned. Never hold the map until the end.
  +> Brevity governs what is WRITTEN into the map. It never governs what is READ. Read every file whose function you record.
  +> Documentation, specifications, READMEs, file names, and folder structure state INTENT. They are not evidence that a functionality exists.
  !> condition := OK on any element or join that was not read at its source. Intent-only records carry UNVERIFIED + note naming what was read instead.
  !> Reporting an intake as complete while any module was not read. Report PARTIAL.
  +> Trace FUNCTIONALITY ONLY.
  !> Genre, medium, encoding, language, style, or any non-functional variant as a namespace segment. (media.photo.jpg, code.cpp, document.word.*, code.engine.game.platformer → INVALID)
  !> Parametrics as elements. Never enumerated, regardless of count.
  !> Solving problems found during trace. MARK and MOVE ON.
  !> Assuming intent before reading intent. !> Assuming the artifact is code.
  !> Prose that can change tomorrow. POINT WITH REFS.
  !> Element reference by readable name. Identity = namespace_address, always.
  !> Duplicate namespace records for an element that is RE in one join and PE in another.
  !> Element-level EF stored outside a join.
  !> Removing an absorbed subpart. It stays an element, held by the parent's join.
  !> Vague top-level labels where a specific functional mechanism exists.
  !> Coined, invented, adapted, colloquial, marketing, or bespoke terms. Industry-standard lexicon; else plain common noun.
  !> CQU := operator | developer (unless AT = code.ide or actual programming tool) | end user | requester of intake.
  !> CQU as an element of the AUE. CQU lives at downstream.cqu.<type address>, role CQU.
  !> Gating or judging intake. Only the resulting map is graded.
  +> Every element carries exactly one role ∈ {Roles}. Upstream elements carry NE.
  +> Every join: receiver(RE) + elements(PE addresses) + purpose(OP) + ef(PE's EF for THIS encounter) + ifd. After phase 2: ≥1 read/spec ref, or a note saying what was looked for.
  +> Refs list is REPLACED on re-record. Send every ref each time.
  +> `name` = canonical name exactly as used in project specifications; fallback = industry term. `name_length` = lookback segment count.
  +> Joins speak about THIS AUE in its own particulars. Representation's function within the AUE, not the real-world thing's.
  +> Seek SE elements for every AUE.
  +> Final shape: ONE root; a named core node contains all elements; nothing free-floating.
  +> AUE too large for one context: LIST every member first; READ in parts; DELEGATE a part to a subordinate reader carrying this procedure; RECORD as each part is read.
  ~> Saying less on many things in the MAP > saying more on one thing. The CQU driving the most improvement yields the best inference.
  ~> Scope transition: zoom into an element and it becomes an entity with subordinate elements.

@CONDITION (INTAKE_STATUS):
  CALL {MCP}.intake.status()
  ?IF ( no intake AND none recording )                    -> {Intake_State} := NONE
  :ELSE ?IF ( one is being recorded )                     -> {Intake_State} := RECORDING
  :ELSE                                                   -> {Intake_State} := ACTIVE

@CONDITION (PROMPT_MODE):
  ?IF ( {Prompt} = NULL OR names only a target )                              -> {Prompt_Mode} := INTAKE
  :ELSE ?IF ( {Prompt} requests verification / re-verification of existing map ) -> {Prompt_Mode} := VERIFY_ONLY
  :ELSE ?IF ( {Prompt} requests refinement/correction of existing map )       -> {Prompt_Mode} := REFINE
  :ELSE ?IF ( {Prompt} requests correction layer construction )               -> {Prompt_Mode} := CORRECTION_LAYER
  :ELSE ?IF ( {Prompt} requests blind spot analysis )                         -> {Prompt_Mode} := BLIND_SPOT
  :ELSE ?IF ( {Prompt} defines new feature/enhancement )                      -> {Prompt_Mode} := FEATURE
  :ELSE                                                                       -> {Prompt_Mode} := OTHER_TASK

@CONDITION (INPUT_KIND):
  ?IF ( {Target} is a folder OR multiple artifacts )      -> {Input_Kind} := FOLDER_OR_COLLECTION
  :ELSE                                                   -> {Input_Kind} := SINGLE_AUE

@CONDITION (SCALE):
  ?IF ( {Members} will not fit one context )              -> DELEGATE: partition {Members} by module; one subordinate reader per module, each carrying this procedure + its slice; orchestrator keeps Root_Join, Closure, Anneal, Proof
  :ELSE                                                   -> SINGLE_READER

@CONDITION (NS_VALID) [every candidate namespace_address]:
  ?IF ( root ∉ {Roots} )                                                             -> INVALID
  ?IF ( reversed segments do not read as a noun phrase with parent as last name )    -> INVALID
  ?IF ( any segment names encoding | language | genre | style | medium | subject-variant ) -> INVALID
  ?IF ( leaf is not a part-of or type-of its parent, or is a non-functionality )     -> INVALID
  ?IF ( underscore-joined segment contains a word that forms a valid prefix alone )  -> INVALID
  ?IF ( any token is coined / non-standard / shorthand / marketing )                 -> INVALID
  ?IF ( address is AUE-specific rather than type-level )                             -> INVALID
  :ELSE                                                                              -> VALID

@CONDITION (CQU_VALID):
  ?IF ( candidate ∈ {operator, developer*, end user, requester} )                    -> INVALID   // *unless AT = code.ide / programming tool
  ?IF ( candidate only judges or records and does not drive change )                 -> INVALID   // buyer, insurance company
  ?IF ( candidate is an element of the AUE )                                         -> INVALID
  ?IF ( candidate is not a type at most-specific reusable level )                    -> INVALID
  ?IF ( holds objective purpose for this artifact type AND drives change/improvement ) -> VALID  // seller, reader, blogger, social media poster
  :ELSE                                                                              -> INVALID

@CONDITION (ROLE_ASSIGN) [per element inside AUE]:
  ?IF ( loss prevents AUE from remaining the same type AND its EF serves external CQU's OP ) -> DE
  :ELSE ?IF ( its EF helps DE serve CQU's OP — even if weak/subversive/replaceable )          -> SE
  :ELSE ?IF ( it defines an essential demand/requirement/dependency )                          -> NE
  :ELSE ?IF ( parametric )                                                                     -> SKIP
  :ELSE                                                                                        -> SKIP (nameable ≠ notable)

@CONDITION (CONDITION_PHASE1) [per element, at record time]:
  ?IF ( source was read AND stated function present and operates )  -> condition := OK ; ADD {Ref_Read}
  :ELSE ?IF ( source was read AND incorrect/incomplete/placeholder ) -> condition := BKN ; note := [what is broken] + [what corrects it]
  :ELSE ?IF ( claimed but absent / unbuilt )                        -> condition := MISS
  :ELSE                                                             -> condition := UNVERIFIED ; note := [what was read in its place]

@CONDITION (CONDITION_PHASE2) [per element, after RESOLVE + READ]:
  ?IF ( no path ref resolves )                                      -> MISS
  :ELSE ?IF ( function stated in its joins is present and operates ) -> OK ; ADD {Ref_Read}
  :ELSE ?IF ( present but incorrect, incomplete, or placeholder )   -> BKN ; note := [what is wrong] + [what corrects it]
  :ELSE ?IF ( source exists, stated function does not )             -> MISS
  // upstream elements: confirmed by declared dependency, not by reading vendor source

@CONDITION (ENCAPSULATE):
  ?IF ( parent's purpose can carry subpart's purpose )    -> ENCAPSULATE (subpart purpose recorded as refinement in its own subtype join)
  :ELSE                                                   -> KEEP INDEPENDENT

@CONDITION (COMPLETE_1):
  ?IF ( {Open_OPs} = [] AND no unnamed NE required AND single root AND core node contains all AND second pass done ) -> {Map_State} := PROOFED_1
  :ELSE -> RECURSE

@CONDITION (COMPLETE_2):
  ?IF ( {Unverified} = []
        AND every OK carries a read ref
        AND every join carries a read/spec ref or a note
        AND every claiming spec record has a corresponding condition
        AND {Untouched} = [] (every member referenced or in {Set_Aside}) ) -> {Map_State} := PROOFED_2
  :ELSE -> RECURSE
  ?IF ( every condition = OK AND count(MISS)=0 AND count(BKN)=0 )         -> PRESUMED_SHALLOW: read back against artifact once more before finish

@ROUTER:
  @MATCH ( {Intake_State}, {Prompt_Mode} ):
    | [NONE,      INTAKE]      -> Boot -> Survey -> Root_Join -> Trace -> Closure -> Anneal -> Proof_1 -> Verify -> Proof_2 -> Finish
    | [RECORDING, INTAKE]      -> Resume -> (continue from {Map_State}) ... -> Finish
    | [ACTIVE,    INTAKE]      -> Resume -> Proof_1 -> Verify -> Proof_2 -> Finish
    | [*,         VERIFY_ONLY] -> Resume -> Verify -> Proof_2 -> Finish          // re-runnable anytime; never repeats phase 1
    | [*,  REFINE | CORRECTION_LAYER | BLIND_SPOT | FEATURE | OTHER_TASK ] -> Resume -> Task_Refine -> Verify (affected slice) -> Proof_2 -> Finish
  @MATCH ( {Input_Kind} ) [within Survey]:
    | [SINGLE_AUE]           -> Survey.[STEP 3] single-path
    | [FOLDER_OR_COLLECTION] -> Survey.[STEP 3] survey-every-member-before-grouping
  @MATCH ( SCALE ) [within Survey and Verify]:
    | [SINGLE_READER] -> same agent reads all
    | [DELEGATE]      -> EXECUTE_PIPELINE( Module_Reader ) per module, in parallel; orchestrator merges via shared intake

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE (Boot):
  [STEP 1]: CALL {MCP}.metaform.register( id ) IF folder not yet a project.
  [STEP 2]: CALL {MCP}.web.start() => RETURN browser address TO USER before intake begins.
  [STEP 3]: CALL {MCP}.intake.schema() ; CALL {MCP}.intake.prompt( text ) => ∇ load roots, links, element and join forms.
  [STEP 4]: CALL {MCP}.intake.start( model, role ) WITH {Result_ID} => intake OPEN. YIELD.

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE (Resume):
  [STEP 1]: CALL {MCP}.intake.start( model, role ) => resume recording.
  [STEP 2]: CALL {MCP}.intake.show( receiver=NULL ) => ∇ existing map into {Recorded}; {Unverified} := elements with condition UNVERIFIED or unset. YIELD.

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE (Survey):                                    // steps 1, 3
  [STEP 1]: ∇({Target}) => {Members} := LIST every file. Load context as if own system prompt. Read intent BEFORE inferring intent. Determine artifact nature (code | document | media | data | unbuilt). Form expectation model: what should exist, what is inferred-but-absent, where drift exists. Mark; do not solve. Apply SCALE.
  [STEP 2]: ∇([STEP 1]) => FOR each AUE: OBSERVE; READ its source where it exists; REASON AT, DE, SE, NE candidates, OP/EF relationships. Apply ROLE_ASSIGN. Apply NS_VALID.
  [STEP 3]: Δ([STEP 2]) => GROUP AUEs into AT groups whose shared functionality supports the same AT-level imperative ( OP of CQU × EF of DE ). IF FOLDER_OR_COLLECTION: survey EVERY member before finalizing groups. Multiples of one type → collection.<type address>, members retained via refs.
  [STEP 4]: RECORD each AUE element immediately: intake.element( namespace_address, name_length, name, role=AUE, refs, within, condition per CONDITION_PHASE1, note ). YIELD.

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE (Root_Join):                                 // step 4 + cqu_entity_rules
  [STEP 1]: ∇(each AT) => Infer CQU type from what the artifact IS. Enumerate every CQU whose purpose drives change; select the one driving the MOST improvement. Apply CQU_VALID. One person, several roles → the role that changes the artifact, by its title.
  [STEP 2]: RECORD intake.element( downstream.cqu.<cqu type address>, name_length, name, role=CQU, ... ).
  [STEP 3]: Δ => Tripartite root join: receiver=downstream.cqu.<...>, elements=[DE address], purpose=CQU's OP, ef=DE's EF, ifd.
            ?IF ( AT has multiple members ) -> CREATE collection element; one {Ref_Member} per member ON the collection; collection with unique CQU gets its own root join under the core node.
            :ELSE -> {Ref_Member} ON the join.
  [STEP 4]: RECORD intake.join( ... ). Apply CONDITION_PHASE1. PUSH DE onto {Open_OPs}. YIELD.

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE (Trace):                                     // steps 5–9, recursive
  [STEP 1]: POP {RE} from {Open_OPs}. {Map_State} := TRACING.
  [STEP 2]: ∇({RE}) => READ its source. FIND its OPs: what it needs from the rest of the AUE or from outside to deliver its own EF. DECOMPOSE requirements as EFs of other elements. DE remains PE to the CQU while acting as RE here.
  [STEP 3]: FOR each requirement:
            ?IF ( outside the AUE ) -> RECORD upstream.<type address>, role=NE, refs=[{Ref_Upstream}].
            :ELSE -> ROLE_ASSIGN; NS_VALID; RECORD element IF not in {Recorded}; condition per CONDITION_PHASE1.
  [STEP 4]: Δ => FOR each PE whose EF serves {RE}'s OP: intake.join( receiver={RE}, elements=[PE], purpose=active OP, ef=PE's EF, ifd, refs IF needed ). One object per call, as reasoned.
  [STEP 5]: ?IF ( encountered element bears its own OP ) -> PUSH onto {Open_OPs} (no duplicate record).
  [STEP 6]: ?IF ( {Open_OPs} ≠ [] ) -> RECURSE [STEP 1]. :ELSE -> YIELD.
  [INVARIANT]: Every OP traces back through receivers to a root join. Parametrics never enter {Open_OPs}.

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE (Closure):                                   // step 10
  [STEP 1]: RETURN to Survey.[STEP 1] expectation model. ∇(AUE functionality set − traced set) => unreached functionalities.
  [STEP 2]: FOR each: FIND the RE whose OP it serves; RECORD the join. ?IF ( only part of a named functionality ) -> parent's join states it.
  [STEP 3]: {Map_State} := CLOSED. YIELD.

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE (Anneal):                                    // step 11
  [STEP 1]: ∇({Recorded}) => PE subfunctions sharing integration joins into one RE's parent function.
  [STEP 2]: Apply ENCAPSULATE per subpart. Encapsulated: remains an element; purpose recorded as refinement in its own subtype join. Independent: untouched.
  [STEP 3]: Δ => Macro-function join carries the combined encounter. NO functionality optimized away. RE-RECORD affected objects (full refs each time). {Map_State} := ANNEALED. YIELD.

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE (Proof_1):                                   // step 12
  [STEP 1]: intake.show( NULL ) => READ the whole map back.
  [STEP 2]: ∇(map × artifact × this process) => CHECK: single root; named core node holds all; nothing free-floating; one role per element; every join has receiver/elements/purpose/ef/ifd; every reference is a namespace_address; NS_VALID everywhere; CQU_VALID everywhere; BKN carries explanation + correction; SE sought per AUE.
  [STEP 3]: CORRECT via re-record or intake.remove( receiver, provider, namespace_address ). ANNEAL again if shape changed.
  [STEP 4]: Apply COMPLETE_1. PROOFED_1 -> {Phase} := 2 ; YIELD -> Verify. :ELSE RECURSE.

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE (Verify):                                    // PHASE 2 — steps 13–17
  [STEP 13]: intake.show( NULL ) => {Recorded}; {Unverified} := every DE/SE/NE inside the AUE with condition UNVERIFIED or unset. {Members} := LIST every file of the project (fresh, not from memory). Apply SCALE → Module_Reader per module if DELEGATE. {Map_State} := VERIFYING.
  [STEP 14]: FOR each element in {Unverified}:
             RESOLVE its path refs. ?IF ( none resolve ) -> MISS.
             :ELSE READ the source. Apply CONDITION_PHASE2.
             RE-RECORD intake.element( ..., condition, refs=[all existing + {Ref_Read}], note ).
             {Report}.per_module[m].read += path. NEXT element.
  [STEP 15]: FOR each join in {Recorded}:
             LOCATE the source where the PE's EF serves the receiver's OP. ADD {Ref_Read} or {Ref_Spec}.
             ?IF ( cannot be located ) -> join.condition := weaker( endpoints' conditions ) ; note := [what was looked for].
             RE-RECORD intake.join( ..., refs=[full list] ). NEXT join.
  [STEP 16]: FOR each specification record claiming a state ( open | deferred | unbuilt | done ):
             FIND its element. ?IF ( none ) -> RECORD element with condition MISS, refs=[{Ref_Spec}].
             ?IF ( element.condition disagrees with record's claim ) -> NOTE drift on the element. NEXT record.
  [STEP 17]: {Untouched} := {Members} − ( every path/read ref in {Recorded} ). FOR each member in {Untouched}:
             READ it. EITHER record its element + the join it serves, OR {Set_Aside}[member] := [one line: parametric | encoding | duplicate of <address> | build output]. NEXT member.
  [STEP 18]: YIELD -> Proof_2.

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE (Module_Reader):                             // subordinate reader; runs Survey/Trace slice or Verify slice for ONE module
  [STEP 1]: RECEIVE: this procedure; module path; {Members} slice; relevant spec records; map slice from intake.show( receiver ∈ module ).
  [STEP 2]: RUN the active phase's pipeline over the slice only. Record into the shared intake, one object per call, as reasoned. Never record outside the slice; report cross-module OPs back to the orchestrator for routing.
  [STEP 3]: RETURN: {Report}.per_module[m] := { read, set_aside, OK, BKN, MISS }. YIELD.

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE (Proof_2):                                   // step 18
  [STEP 1]: intake.show( NULL ) => READ the whole map back.
  [STEP 2]: Apply COMPLETE_2. ?IF PRESUMED_SHALLOW -> read back against the artifact once more; re-apply CONDITION_PHASE2 to a sample across every module.
  [STEP 3]: CORRECT; RE-RECORD. ?IF ( not PROOFED_2 ) -> RECURSE Verify on the remaining queue. :ELSE YIELD -> Finish.

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE (Finish):
  [STEP 1]: Δ({Report}) => by module: what was read, what was set aside, count OK / BKN / MISS.
  [STEP 2]: ?IF ( any module not read ) -> {Report}.partial := TRUE ; state it. Never report complete.
  [STEP 3]: CALL intake.finish( report, feedback ) => recorded metaform becomes active. YIELD {Result_ID}.

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE (Task_Refine):                               // {Prompt} is a task on an existing intake
  [STEP 1]: ∇({Prompt}, {Recorded}) => isolate scope: receivers, elements, joins touched.
  [STEP 2]: @MATCH ( {Prompt_Mode} ):
            | [REFINE]           -> re-run Trace on affected REs; re-record
            | [CORRECTION_LAYER] -> FOR each BKN/MISS: record correction-path notes on element and joins
            | [BLIND_SPOT]       -> re-run Closure against a fresh expectation model; record unreached functionality
            | [FEATURE]          -> record inferred-but-unbuilt elements as MISS with intent notes and joins to their REs
            | [OTHER_TASK]       -> apply all constraints; route to nearest pipeline
  [STEP 3]: YIELD -> Verify (affected slice) -> Proof_2 -> Finish.

@VERIFY:
  Was every element and join recorded via an intake call at the moment it was reasoned?                              If NO -> HALT; record pending objects; RECURSE.
  Is any element or join marked OK without a read ref?                                                               If YES -> condition := UNVERIFIED; RECURSE Verify.[STEP 14].
  Was any element recorded from README / spec / names / structure alone and NOT marked UNVERIFIED with a note?       If YES -> re-record; RECURSE.
  Is {Unverified} ≠ [] at Finish?                                                                                    If YES -> HALT; RECURSE Verify.
  Is any member of {Members} neither referenced nor in {Set_Aside}?                                                   If YES -> RECURSE Verify.[STEP 17].
  Does any spec record claiming a state lack a corresponding condition?                                              If YES -> RECURSE Verify.[STEP 16].
  Does any join lack a read/spec ref AND lack a note?                                                                If YES -> RECURSE Verify.[STEP 15].
  Is every condition OK with zero MISS and zero BKN?                                                                 If YES -> PRESUMED_SHALLOW; read back against artifact; RECURSE Proof_2.
  Does any namespace segment name genre, medium, encoding, language, style, or a parametric?                         If YES -> intake.remove; RECURSE NS_VALID.
  Is any CQU = operator | developer (non-tool AT) | end user | requester, or an element of the AUE?                    If YES -> RECURSE Root_Join.[STEP 1].
  Does every element carry exactly one role, upstream = NE, CQU under downstream.cqu.*?                               If NO -> re-record.
  Does every join carry receiver, elements (addresses), purpose, ef, ifd?                                              If NO -> re-record.
  Does any reference use a readable name instead of a namespace_address?                                              If YES -> re-record.
  Does every OP trace back through receivers to a root join?                                                           If NO -> RECURSE Trace.
  Was any problem solved instead of marked? Any BKN without explanation + correction?                                 If YES -> correct note; RECURSE.
  Exactly one root, named core node holding everything, nothing free-floating?                                        If NO -> RECURSE Proof_1.
  Was brevity applied to READING rather than to WRITING (files skipped, modules unread)?                              If YES -> {Report}.partial := TRUE; RECURSE Verify on unread modules.
  Does the finish report state, by module, what was read, what was set aside, and OK/BKN/MISS counts?                 If NO -> rebuild {Report}; RECURSE Finish.
  ALL PASS -> intake.finish( report, feedback ) -> YIELD {Result_ID}.
